reasons={
'ui_pixels':('retain','medium-high lexical and contextual','The AOSP paired camera records attest the exact plural ፒክሰሎች. Removing the explicit camera quantity leaves the generic unit without introducing a resize, crop, normalization, DPI or screen-density meaning. A bare plural is suitable for the unit choice. This is a justified component extraction, not an exact standalone AOSP label. LibreOffice alternatives are not silently normalized.'),
'ui_percent':('retain','high lexical; medium-high contextual','LibreOffice has an exact nonfuzzy Percent label with ፐርሰንት in two contexts. The candidate names the unit alone, so it survives every inspected percentage baseline. The AOSP native alternative መቶኛ is legitimate but is not evidence that this loanword is wrong.'),
'ui_pixels_6ec9c2':('retain','medium-high lexical; complete spoken phrase pending','Retain the exact attested plural as a bare unit resource. It has no preposition, number, screen-density meaning or fixed baseline. It can be combined with the template without duplicated በ. This lexical retention does not clear the held Width/Height-in compositions; whether a singular measure-word is more idiomatic in those phrases remains open.'),
'ui_percent_fd8671':('retain','high lexical; complete spoken phrase pending','Retain the same denominator-neutral percent noun. The LibreOffice in-percent prose supports use with በ, and the resource correctly does not contain that preposition itself. English capitalization does not require distinct Amharic values or permit merging the separate keys. Full spoken-label acceptance is withheld with the templates.'),
'ui_width':('retain','high noun evidence; medium-high composed-label confidence','The AOSP image-details Width record and LibreOffice graphics Width record agree on ስፋት. Both static results, ስፋት (px) and ስፋት (%), are clear noun-plus-parenthetical-unit labels. There is no unit inflection across the parenthesis boundary. The argument remains a unit token, not a numeric value.'),
'ui_height':('retain','high image-noun evidence; medium-high composed-label confidence','The exact paired AOSP image-details Height record supports ቁመት in this image-dimension context. Both ቁመት (px) and ቁመት (%) retain that meaning without action or area semantics. LibreOffice እርዝመት remains a genuine alternative, but the more directly paired image evidence supports retaining the proposed noun rather than forcing a revision.'),
'ui_width_in':('hold','medium semantic plausibility; insufficient complete-label idiom confidence','The two results are semantically intelligible: ስፋት በፒክሰሎች and ስፋት በፐርሰንት. The attached በ is structurally plausible, occurs exactly once, and is supported by AOSP unit-preposition usage. However, the preserved pixel/percent precedents are finite prose, and the AOSP seconds example is an imperative. They do not settle the naturalness of this noun-first short accessibility label or the plural versus singular pixel measure-word in it. Supplemental LibreOffice width-as-percentage prose corroborates the sequence but still does not settle the label idiom. Hold the exact candidate, do not invent a replacement or call it incorrect.'),
'ui_height_in':('hold','medium semantic plausibility; insufficient complete-label idiom confidence','The results ቁመት በፒክሰሎች and ቁመት በፐርሰንት preserve height and the intended units. Placeholder, preposition and bare-noun integration are structurally sound. Whole-label naturalness and pixel measure-word choice remain unresolved for the same reason as Width-in; the additional height-as-percentage prose uses the alternative እርዝመት, not this exact noun. Hold this candidate and retain that alternative for a coordinated contextual decision. No grammatical defect is proved and no stronger replacement is established.')}
